        "original_id": "870d9795-e373-5d19-8d70-4f01af1796a4",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Plants: Camassia, Chelone\n- Places: Camas County, Idaho\n- Concepts: asparagus family, eastern North America, Canada, United States, camas root\n\nFacts:\n- Camassia is a genus of plants in the asparagus family native to Canada and the United States.\n- Chelone is a genus of four species of perennial herbaceous plants native to eastern North America.\n- Camas County, Idaho, is named for the camas root, or Camassia, a lily-like plant with an edible bulb found in the region.\n- Native Americans and settlers used the edible bulb of Camassia as a food source in the Camas County, Idaho, region.",
